      "author": {
        "id": 6612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-12T00:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is because the original algorithm is defined only for two arguments and does not generalize directly to the variadic case. In particular, its guard can discard one small argument using a two-term error bound, whereas multiple arguments require accounting for accumulated squared-term errors.",
